Advanced fluid dynamics — Mei notes and MIT modules (@fd-mei: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_21NXVH78F0NYDPDVTG66PG261P
Chiang C. Mei's notes and the MIT fluids modules. [Lecture-note archive](https://web.mit.edu/1.63/www/lecnote.html) · [Modular programme](https://web.mit.edu/fluids-modules/www/) · [Course context](https://web.mit.edu/1.63/www/).

Follow complete relevant chapters on governing laws, creeping and high-Reynolds-number flow, dispersion, porous media, waves, rotation, stratification and instability. Use each module's own assumptions and mathematical preparation. Develop an analytical solution and a changed-condition test for each main approximation studied.

The course landing page describes Spring 2014 instruction by T. R. Akylas, with Peko Hosoi, and notes by Mei. Individual notes include older dates, including 2002; neither date should be silently assigned to every file. The modules explicitly include unfinished areas. Public notes do not establish a complete video, assessment or software archive. Inspect linked items and their notices; no blanket OCW licence is inferred for this separate MIT site.

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics sources — books, courses, methods and physical evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3Y3TVV9VQAB50M2ZSECK5JTYVG).
